Question Title: Create a Project Folder Structure

Question Link:
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/jipp2htnvrww?lecture_hash=v210chxjexei

Solution:
cat > create-service << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

mkdir -p service/controllers
mkdir -p service/models
mkdir -p service/routes
mkdir -p service/middleware

echo "API Service" > service/README.md
echo 'console.log("Server started");' > service/server.js
EOF

chmod +x create-service
./create-service

Approach:
1. Writing the correct code in create-service replacing the original wrong code

2. Giving create-service execution permission 

3. Executing create-service to create the required service srtucture

Result:
service/
├── controllers/
├── models/
├── routes/
├── middleware/
├── server.js
└── README.md
service structure obtained